   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# TV Power Off\n\nEnds a scene like a switched-off tube: the picture squashes into a bright horizontal line, the line pinches to a phosphor dot, the dot fades and the frame is dead black. Runs its WebGL shader over its own built-in scene (a render queue list; title, rows and background from variables), not over the host video. Plays once: 25 frames of picture, an 18-frame collapse, then black.\n\nCategory: effects. Length: 2.0667 s. WebGL: yes.\n\nUse when:\n- A scene should end like a device being switched off rather than fading out.\n- The video is about something that lives on a screen (a terminal, a dashboard, a retro build) and powering it down is the punctuation.\n- A beat needs a hard end: everything after the collapse is black.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The tube look should hold for the whole scene instead of ending it: use crt-screen.\n- Both scenes should be visible while the change happens: reach for a transition such as glitch-cut.\n- The frame has to stay transparent once the scene is gone: what this leaves behind is opaque black.\n\nVariables:\n- title (string): Title, default \"Render queue\"\n- items (string): Rows, default \"intro-scene.mp4 | Done; feature-tour.mp4 | Rendering; pricing-outro.mp4 | Queued\"\n- background (color): Background, default \"#101828\"\n- delay (number, 0-60): Delay, default 25\n- length (number, 8-30): Length, default 18\n- gain (number, 0-2): Gain, default 1\n- afterglow (number, 0-2): Afterglow, default 1\n- phosphor (color): Phosphor, default \"#d8ecff\"\n- resolution (number, 0.25-1): Resolution, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
